          1,
          1.05
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Entonces Hiʻiaka abrazó a Lohiʻau y lo besó, nariz con nariz, como se besaba en el antiguo Hawaiʻi.",
          "en": "Then Hiʻiaka threw her arms around Lohiʻau and kissed him, nose to nose, the old Hawaiian way."
        },
        {
          "es": "«¡Miren!», gritaron las mujeres de Pele. «¡Hiʻiaka besa a tu hombre!»",
          "en": "\"Look!\" cried Pele's women. \"Hiʻiaka is kissing your man!\""
        },
        {
          "es": "Al principio, Pele hizo como si nada. «Para eso se hizo la nariz», dijo.",
          "en": "At first, Pele acted as if it were nothing. \"The nose was made for kissing,\" she said."
        },
        {
          "es": "Pero cuando los vio abrazados, su cara se endureció. «Quémenlo», ordenó.",
          "en": "But when she saw them in each other's arms, her face turned hard. \"Burn him,\" she ordered."
        }
      ],
